course: dictionary
lesson: 2541
title: Defend: protect, speak up, or stop a goal
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Defend is a verb, and it has several meanings. To defend something is to protect it from attack or harm. To defend an idea or a friend is to speak up for them. In sport, to defend is to try to stop the other team scoring.
explain: «Bees and wasps sting mainly to defend themselves and their nest.» Here defend means protect. The sting is how they guard themselves and their home. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "Bees sting mainly to protect themselves and their nest" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Check the other senses the same way. «The robin was defending its patch all winter» means it was protecting its territory from other robins, not that it was speaking up for them. Read the words around the word, and you will know which sense the author means.
fact: Defend is a verb: defend, defends, defended, defending.
fact: «Defend» means to protect someone or something from attack or harm.
fact: «Defend» can also mean to speak up in support of someone or an idea.
fact: In sport, a defender tries to stop the other team scoring.
fact: Useful phrases: defend yourself, defend against, defend a goal, defend someone's opinion.
exercise: «Red wood ants bite and spray a stinging acid to defend their nest mounds.» What does defend mean here? | To build a new nest somewhere else | To leave the nest and go away | To count the ants in the nest | *To protect from attack or harm
exercise: Sam says he will defend his friend who is being bullied by telling a teacher. What does defend mean here? | To run away from the problem | To forget about it quickly | *To speak up for someone and protect them | To copy what the bully does
exercise: In a football match, the defender runs back to defend the goal. What does defend mean in sport? | *To try to stop the other team scoring | To pass the ball to the goalkeeper | To watch the crowd from the pitch | To score a goal for their own team
test: «The mother bear is ___ her cub from the other bears.» Which word fills the gap? | defended | defends | *defending | defend
test: Which sentence uses defend to mean speak up for an idea? | *She stood up to defend her idea in the class debate. | She drew a picture of a castle on the wall. | He ate his lunch quickly. | The swan ran across the lake.
exam: The grass snake «defends itself by hissing, giving off a bad smell or playing dead.» What does defend mean here? | To make a new home in the grass | To swim to the other side of the pond | *To protect itself from harm | To eat frogs for dinner
